cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Dominant migration strategies within the Gulf of St. Lawrence capelin stock inferred from otolith chemistry transects"
abstract: >-
  R code implementing the full analysis pipeline used to infer dominant
  migration strategies of Gulf of St. Lawrence capelin from otolith
  chemistry transects: QDA-based region assignment along each transect,
  multi-resolution binning and sensitivity analyses on the transition
  threshold, Multiple Correspondence Analysis (MCA) and k-means clustering
  of individual migration histories, and comparison of resulting clusters
  with trawl-survey fork-length distributions.
type: software
